## Lore

A military doctor in the armed forces of the New German Republic, roughly the Body Fixer''s equivalent with basic military training behind it. A capable surgeon and healer used to combat conditions and makeshift operating rooms.

Most medical personnel avoid combat and concentrate on saving lives; some refuse to carry firearms at all. All are trained in self defence and the energy rifle whether they use them or not, and all are dangerous with a scalpel or knife. Most travel light in light body armour, giving priority to medical equipment.

Alignment: Any ' || char(8212) || ' good, selfish or evil.

## Skill penalties the GM applies

The medical officer is at -20% whenever working on bionic modification or installation, and at -40% on extremely alien physiology, bionics, bio-wizard symbiotes or implants, or Mindwerks brain implants. Both are conditional and are not stored as skill bonuses.

## Rank and pay

All doctors and medical officers start at the rank of captain. Salary is 3000 credits a month, rising to 4200 for ninth level and higher, with quarters, food, clothing and medical access provided. Out of the field the officer gets a private apartment near a hospital or on a base.

## Cybernetics

Select two cybernetic augmentations from any category at creation, usually sensory. Favoured types are lung, eye and sensor implants. Not stored, because the choice is unrestricted and the catalog has no cybernetics picker.

## GM Notes

A medical officer who leaves the military and turns rogue continues to advance under this O.C.C. without penalty. Association with mutants, D-bees, vagabonds, mercenaries, gypsies and men of magic is a serious crime in the NGR and is frequently judged an act of treason.

The character can also function as a field scientist depending on the other skills selected.

Equipment available upon assignment includes the one-man XM-50 medical ambulance, other medivac transport, additional weapons, ammunition, medical supplies and nano-bots, a robot assistant, medical assistants, and access to hospitals, laboratories, operating rooms, computers, military escort, rations and field equipment. Medical officers are usually given priority for medical supplies.
